# Operator task injection from the dashboard — FR-DASH-5 (docs/PRD.md:526-534).

# 'prospect' | 'excavate' | 'haul'. Anything else is rejected outright
# (MANUAL_TASK_CAPABILITIES, orchestrator_node.py:112-116, tested at :414).
string task_type

# Target in world metres. z is unused.
geometry_msgs/Point target_location

# KILOGRAMS. Meaning depends on task_type:
#   excavate -- target extracted mass for this task
#   haul     -- target delivered mass for this task
#   prospect -- IGNORED; a survey has no mass. A non-zero value is accepted and
#               the response message says it was ignored.
# 0.0 means unconstrained: fill to the robot's own RCDL capacity, which is the
# behaviour before this field was read at all. Negative or non-finite is
# rejected. NOT clamped here — the orchestrator has no HAL and no RCDL; the
# agent clamps against selene_hal/config/<type>.yaml (excavator hopper_fill
# capacity_kg 20, hauler load_cell capacity_kg 50).
float32 quantity

# OPTIONAL, and a PREFERENCE — not a force-assignment.
# The task enters the auction like any other (docs/PRD.md:533, FR-DASH-5(b)).
# If this robot bids it wins regardless of score; if it does not bid within
# inject_preferred_robot_max_rounds auctions the preference is dropped with a
# WARNING alert and the auction opens up.
# It is NOT a way to pre-empt a busy robot. Use OverrideRobot 'cancel_task'
# first — that path is logged and appears in the task history, and it works: the
# old force-assign path published a TaskAssignment that agent_node.py:682-688
# discards for any robot not in BIDDING or ASSIGNED, i.e. exactly the busy robot
# it was meant to serve, after having already re-PENDed that robot's task.
string assigned_robot_id
---
bool success
string task_id
string message
